      "status": "passed",
      "score": 4.6,
      "rounds": 1,
      "findings": [
        {
          "criterion": "actionable-steps",
          "score": 3,
          "finding": "Step 2 (\"Write the embedder\", module body): the opening heredoc line `cat > /lab/embed.py <<'PY'` is shown twice — once as the tab-indented backticked command and again as the first line of the plain heredoc block that immediately follows. The step instructs the reader to \"type or paste it exactly as shown\", so a reader who runs the backticked line and then pastes the block writes the cat line into /lab/embed.py as the first line of the Python file, and the step-3 run fails with a syntax error. Missing: a single non-duplicated presentation of the lines to enter, or an explicit instruction that only the body (from `import json, math` through the closing `PY`) is what gets pasted."
        },
        {
